slope field at the points $(1,-1)$,$(0,-2)$,$(-2,2)$.\n\nTo sketch the slope field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the right-hand side of the differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(1,-1)}=\\frac{5}{2}-3(1)(-1)=\\frac{5}{2}-(-3)=\\frac{11}{2}, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(0,-2)}=\\frac{5}{2}-3(0)(-2)=\\frac{5}{2}-(0)=\\frac{5}{2}, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-2,2)}=\\frac{5}{2}-3(-2)(2)=\\frac{5}{2}-(-12)=\\frac{29}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting up our points and drawing our line segments, we get the following diagram.\n\n![](images/f7/f77d4f1780e4ff74fce5e0303564f38a77968bd2e56390603a9b5b97f03b39a9.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526361 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "009fad15-5d1a-5691-9dbb-aa0e0c3f2c51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/92/921545ac305c978db5f35718ddcc60aea6240a4bf0c92e3134649e944bbceeb1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526299} {:answer/id #uuid "027dcc9c-6cc1-5c14-beb5-3f82d7071dd3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/bb/bbe64090631ee780d071785a8f97a8870dd2f6557746e2ed7395e9db6e326b48.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526300} {:answer/id #uuid "2e976e20-a065-57ab-8f05-59b325938a8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/7a/7a323280b383e42c19701d86c4b005a769ae33539b380fa72e74b117629daac3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526316} {:answer/id #uuid "b632995b-2aa6-549d-a84f-ba75faa988eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/52/527b523863037a491a2adf844ad97a183e26eb76db708d931b1f6baac31c10c7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526348} {:answer/id #uuid "e51273cd-2b6f-50e1-87c1-939e753b8e95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ca/ca18948802d9d78a214c7fe1c311b070dd75cb34cf1a86e419a11327dce67c6a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526359}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e976e20-a065-57ab-8f05-59b325938a8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/7a/7a323280b383e42c19701d86c4b005a769ae33539b380fa72e74b117629daac3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526316} :answer-field/id #uuid "368b9ac6-233e-5c72-a838-3c8d9640927d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526319}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ec562691-61f7-5234-8201-f633bff4db89" :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams gives the slope field at the points indicated for the differential equation $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2}x^{2}-(-1)y^{2}?\n$$" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "We have to sketch the slope field at the points $(-2,-1)$,$(2,-2)$,$(-1,3)$.\n\nTo sketch the slope field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the right-hand side of the differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-2,-1)}=\\frac{1}{2}(-2)^{2}-(-1)(-1)^{2}=2-(-1)=3, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(2,-2)}=\\frac{1}{2}(2)^{2}-(-1)(-2)^{2}=2-(-4)=6, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-1,3)}=\\frac{1}{2}(-1)^{2}-(-1)(3)^{2}=\\frac{1}{2}-(-9)=\\frac{19}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting up our points and drawing our line segments, we get the following diagram.\n\n![](images/7a/7a323280b383e42c19701d86c4b005a769ae33539b380fa72e74b117629daac3.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186670666 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2275f5fa-bafb-572f-b6e7-d370b905f9ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/20/20e196260d4d38071108e0dbb55879348386b1eb2b502fa3b6b4423f0e367339.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670667} {:answer/id #uuid "2671a4fc-1fbc-5996-a738-9b8b5cce8b0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/bf/bf2a18117030301e91784f141d5601a9971f1c6902b2ea6236f2f6b1773f53dd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670668} {:answer/id #uuid "2eda0ba7-6e23-5033-867a-c0062bad0c84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/24/24a904a600c6475d1274fa7b9e06dbed168e0ceec72c0d02b7c31dfdc3431292.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670671} {:answer/id #uuid "547596f5-e0bd-55eb-967b-d130fc7d15d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/cf/cf3ae6090229f1b66486c3606840c74a07be0a37559e06bd3429dec9c458a070.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670678} {:answer/id #uuid "7762a69f-5289-5df8-bc84-20c5c2b08429" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/dc/dcf4fa83568b9f4e85e4f8bf1f123b1bfc77b534ad23f452a80d12f8579fed37.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670685}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2671a4fc-1fbc-5996-a738-9b8b5cce8b0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/bf/bf2a18117030301e91784f141d5601a9971f1c6902b2ea6236f2f6b1773f53dd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670668} :answer-field/id #uuid "da0ed405-0b07-554e-89ea-aa5037d1c790" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670693}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1c183240-5cb2-5523-9f74-95fbf751d6a2" :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams gives the slope field at the points indicated for the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1x+(2)y?$" :question/worked-solution "We have to sketch the slope field at the points $(0,1)$,$(-2,0)$,$(2,-1)$.\n\nTo sketch the slope field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the right-hand side of the differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(0,1)}=1(0)+(2)(1)=2, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-2,0)}=1(-2)+(2)(0)=-2, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(2,-1)}=1(2)+(2)(-1)=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting up our points and drawing our line segments, we get the following diagram.\n\n![](images/bf/bf2a18117030301e91784f141d5601a9971f1c6902b2ea6236f2f6b1773f53dd.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186670673 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26df92e3-988b-5df6-ba53-422e333c817f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f3/f3e940bbe3cf1a82d47a401fef015f4970fab7016f5e82c3bbed5b254251937b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670669} {:answer/id #uuid "2bb5f7ba-f70f-56d8-b156-55d1430c841f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/1d/1dd1a2bade9c53b136f6f66e3b3affe033a51c25dee9eb800412f81ab63c68f1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670670} {:answer/id #uuid "4e721f05-03da-5b8a-ad50-2d1b49465988" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/7d/7d47d65a715204c6b220483ef4373d3f7cf066812f6265f34f8b90be599fd2b0.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670676} {:answer/id #uuid "b8e3ed97-bf7f-5b34-b279-c97fd94002d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/9f/9f25d342472d01ef2cb83116734306cea5fc24be2788aae5527d5addae247348.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670689} {:answer/id #uuid "dcc42b79-e51c-599e-b009-ba59470c42bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f5/f51fb78a12bc37626954936b6f001ff807b97c0c55279314ec60f61ecbfde501.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670694}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dcc42b79-e51c-599e-b009-ba59470c42bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f5/f51fb78a12bc37626954936b6f001ff807b97c0c55279314ec60f61ecbfde501.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670694} :answer-field/id #uuid "68c72f0a-65e2-56fe-82e3-72824b7a97b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670681}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3cf19cc1-07eb-5993-9bf4-76492a205588" :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams gives the slope field at the points indicated for the differential equation $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{(-2)x+(-2)y}{4}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We have to sketch the slope field at the points $(-2,3)$,$(-1,-1)$,$(-3,-1)$.\n\nTo sketch the slope field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the right-hand side of the differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-2,3)}=\\frac{(-2)(-2)+(-2)(3)}{4}=- \\frac{1}{2}, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-1,-1)}=\\frac{(-2)(-1)+(-2)(-1)}{4}=1, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-3,-1)}=\\frac{(-2)(-3)+(-2)(-1)}{4}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting up our points and drawing our line segments, we get the following diagram.\n\n![](images/f5/f51fb78a12bc37626954936b6f001ff807b97c0c55279314ec60f61ecbfde501.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186670674 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f0aa562-4688-530b-b347-e9b9102470e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e1/e1be85524cc3bf86663fead888ea9ebdcaa20f428b874158b90f00910457cbd8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670683} {:answer/id #uuid "7440c7af-6b05-50b5-9966-ccd777778058" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/67/67b130d9506d2f6d2c10b11ddc15f7f95997b27e87453830b089be3a28f548e5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670684} {:answer/id #uuid "7eccabd6-fda5-5243-bac7-bc528f7d0e5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/32/32e3100ae5bf3015985eb7008939c247158687afbdc7f71d76e3278503758ea1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670687} {:answer/id #uuid "bc622d87-4aca-55d3-8289-82c6e42dc4ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b9/b91833eba8558d82b86f66bbc5889f2a6bb2187178170846c12238a3027cd2a0.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670690} {:answer/id #uuid "e2409837-db05-5003-9e2b-cebcba5ff9eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/1e/1ead395d1098618c55a1f1491e8e8ec1079d63a51573e5d138b7c2e4792f2531.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670695}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc622d87-4aca-55d3-8289-82c6e42dc4ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b9/b91833eba8558d82b86f66bbc5889f2a6bb2187178170846c12238a3027cd2a0.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670690} :answer-field/id #uuid "f028d653-d6a4-57e9-987d-557542a2d515" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670697}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "459e46c9-4184-5656-bb8b-3280b2551168" :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams gives the slope field at the points indicated for the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=3x^{2}-(3)y?$" :question/worked-solution "We have to sketch the slope field at the points $(-2,0)$,$(-1,-1)$,$(-1,3)$.\n\nTo sketch the slope field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the right-hand side of the differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-2,0)}=3(-2)^{2}-3(0)=12, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-1,-1)}=3(-1)^{2}-3(-1)=6, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-1,3)}=3(-1)^{2}-3(3)=-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting up our points and drawing our line segments, we get the following diagram.\n\n![](images/b9/b91833eba8558d82b86f66bbc5889f2a6bb2187178170846c12238a3027cd2a0.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186670675 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "123e4d64-73d1-5418-876b-e5811c5c14d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e1/e1a05ebab1bd4eeba5fc91126badf4600fed0cb7e6fc19b848d91e06664f3b1c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670663} {:answer/id #uuid "1532a0cc-56c3-55b3-9723-046ecc0679fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/dd/dde7cf2388af8e602ca6308eeedd2560dc09e1a6062166ce3cef4f69d62d0643.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670665} {:answer/id #uuid "52188b34-0248-5085-a960-b7d7eec72d11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/42/42df4bf8c25e644e5ddfc47623e2e7a391d897ed8ceeb72b429f0b29e5fca2f1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670677} {:answer/id #uuid "614f69c6-32c6-597d-b91d-125f3574b8d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/da/da38e55a37f775b3e531b61436ff070901cd88f7ce4a7c9229f096e87159c3c8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670680} {:answer/id #uuid "69b99694-a609-53a7-b152-6496f8a3e0b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0e/0ee119f4b38461acc0fdb9e529e7e7b53f74c7ead8097e82adcf5fabf1247ede.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670682}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "614f69c6-32c6-597d-b91d-125f3574b8d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/da/da38e55a37f775b3e531b61436ff070901cd88f7ce4a7c9229f096e87159c3c8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670680} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8047dff-ac54-5be9-b9a6-01210efeb5b7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670688}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4a81fec4-e469-52d1-b3ae-2d2d1e2bd280" :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams gives the slope field at the points indicated for the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-1-(2)xy?$" :question/worked-solution "We have to sketch the slope field at the points $(3,-2)$,$(2,-2)$,$(0,-2)$.\n\nTo sketch the slope field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the right-hand side of the differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(3,-2)}=-1-2(3)(-2)=11, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(2,-2)}=-1-2(2)(-2)=7, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(0,-2)}=-1-2(0)(-2)=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting up our points and drawing our line segments, we get the following diagram.\n\n![](images/da/da38e55a37f775b3e531b61436ff070901cd88f7ce4a7c9229f096e87159c3c8.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186670691 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1311b306-fa54-5df7-bd97-0195c638d681" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/13/136c6747f77070e1b5c479f1bbbcaa50ce0d46ddc46fb078f82d76fac1c6ac8a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670664} {:answer/id #uuid "56d25aaf-37ff-585d-9a1c-dcf9044262ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f9/f99bc2a1d6becc2fe69d65bc6d9b83412e4f6f225059ba65953fbf5c84cca41d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670679} {:answer/id #uuid "7a503b6e-f79f-5a2b-b63a-1cf5c3a6d4d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/4e/4eb22b486ec2b341d61458230220e25882af65cfeace3d8e05e4bc22b2670baa.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670686} {:answer/id #uuid "d86e019b-9da1-5397-88a9-493515bec680" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/bb/bb47071e129428930cdf7878017ffac817986a8a9d913e15f98f5a9fa285388c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670692} {:answer/id #uuid "e7b326d0-4853-5a6d-94ad-c20c8fd6f31f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f3/f3e9db617e68f21ff03b3d5bf57764da9d6a0ddd81f18f718cc2c47b60c35eac.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670696}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e7b326d0-4853-5a6d-94ad-c20c8fd6f31f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f3/f3e9db617e68f21ff03b3d5bf57764da9d6a0ddd81f18f718cc2c47b60c35eac.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670696} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a7cf8f3-cfdc-56de-beb7-f60dffef252c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670672}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bcfa9b0d-38a3-51ff-9ca0-b824a54272e1" :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams gives the slope field at the points indicated for the differential equation $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{(-2)x+(2)y}{3}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We have to sketch the slope field at the points $(2,3)$,$(-1,2)$,$(-2,3)$.\n\nTo sketch the slope field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the right-hand side of the differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(2,3)}=\\frac{(-2)(2)+(2)(3)}{3}=\\frac{2}{3}, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-1,2)}=\\frac{(-2)(-1)+(2)(2)}{3}=2, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-2,3)}=\\frac{(-2)(-2)+(2)(3)}{3}=\\frac{10}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting up our points and drawing our line segments, we get the following diagram.\n\n![](images/f3/f3e9db617e68f21ff03b3d5bf57764da9d6a0ddd81f18f718cc2c47b60c35eac.png)"}] :knowledge-point/title "Sketching the Slope Field of a Differential Equation at Some Isolated Points"}]}
